Signed-off-by: Sudeep Holla <sudeep.holla@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Arnd Bergmann <arnd@arndb.de>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the lack of support for the SP810 System Controller in the device tree, which resulted in incorrect clock frequencies being used for the SP804 timers. The timers were not able to select the appropriate clock sources (1MHz or 32kHz) as intended, leading to potential timing issues in the system.

